{
  "id": "h3",
  "order": 3,
  "title": "Five-finger position: right hand",
  "summary": "One finger on each of five white keys.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Five-finger position",
      "body": "**Five-finger position**: each of your five fingers rests over its own key, on five white keys side by side. From there you can play any of those keys without moving your hand.\n\nWith your right thumb on middle C (the C nearest the middle of the keyboard) your fingers cover C, D, E, F and G. This is called C position, after the key under the thumb.\n\n**Why it matters:** many first tunes fit inside one position, so you can play them without looking down or jumping around.",
      "hands": [
        {
          "hand": "right",
          "keys": [
            60,
            62,
            64,
            65,
            67
          ]
        }
      ],
